+# patches/ — dsh-side changes this plugin needs
+
+Source patches against the DeepSeek Harness checkout, kept here because the
+plugin's documented behavior is not complete without them. Apply from the
+harness repository root:
+
+```sh
+git apply patches/dsh-client-entry-config.patch   # from the plugin repository root
+# or, from a harness checkout:
+git apply /path/to/plugin/patches/dsh-client-entry-config.patch
+```
+
+| Patch | Target | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `dsh-client-entry-config.patch` | dsh `0.1.2-alpha.2` (`packages/client/modules`, `packages/client/web`) | The bundle row's `config` block is the plugin's configuration entry point (README §Configuration), and the documented cordis contract is that a plugin's own row config arrives in its own `apply(ctx, config)`. A `dsh.client` browser row is a separate Loader entry created with `loader.create({ name })`, and `WebBootEntry` carries no `config`, so the browser half never receives it. The patch adds an opt-in `dsh.client.config: true` declaration and carries the row's JSON-safe config onto the browser entry. |
+
+`package.json` declares `"dsh.client": { "config": true }` so the plugin opts in
+once the patch is applied; a harness without the field ignores the extra key, and
+the host half's `webserver/index-inject` relay keeps the same three fields
+flowing to the browser half until then.
+
+The patch is a proposal to the harness maintainers, not a published artifact:
+see `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/dsh-client-entry-config/report.md` in the
+migration run for the discussion draft, the search record, and the open
+questions (naming, wire trust surface, test placement).
